course: dictionary
lesson: 9842
title: Swiss: a word about a place and its people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Swiss is a word about a place. When it comes before a noun, like «Swiss chocolate» or «Swiss Alps», it tells you the thing is from, or is about, Switzerland. Switzerland is a small mountain country in the middle of Europe.
explain: Look at the words around it to work out how it is being used. «The Swiss farmers» have a capital S and the word the in front, so Swiss is being used as a noun for the people of Switzerland. «Swiss roll» and «Swiss Army knife» are names, so Swiss is just part of the name.
explain: Context helps you spot the Swiss who are people. In «In 1957 a BBC television programme showed Swiss farmers picking spaghetti from trees», the word Swiss tells you where the farmers came from, even though the story was a joke that many viewers believed.
fact: Swiss means from or about Switzerland, a small mountain country in the middle of Europe.
fact: The Swiss are the people of Switzerland.
fact: Swiss is also used in names: Swiss cheese, Swiss roll and Swiss Army knife.
fact: Switzerland has the Alps and lakes, four official languages and no coastline.
fact: Switzerland is famous for staying neutral in wars.
exercise: «The Rhine flows from the Swiss Alps to the North Sea.» What does Swiss tell you here? | It means the river is very fast | *It tells you the mountains are in Switzerland | It means the sea is cold | It tells you the river is in Spain
exercise: «In 1957 a BBC television programme showed Swiss farmers picking spaghetti from trees.» Who are the Swiss farmers? | *Farmers from Switzerland | Farmers who sell pasta in Italy | Farmers who only grow spaghetti | Farmers who live beside the North Sea
exercise: Which of these is a name that uses the word Swiss? | Scotch egg | Italian ice cream | *Swiss Army knife
test: «Swiss chocolate» is chocolate from which country? | Belgium | *Switzerland | Austria | Germany
test: What does «the Swiss» mean? | Dogs that live in the mountains | The lakes in the Alps | *The people of Switzerland | A kind of cheese
exam: Which is true about Switzerland? | It has only one language | It is in Africa | *It has four official languages | It has a coastline on the sea
